    "### Classification Performance\n",
    "\n",
    "::: {.callout-important title=\"In-sample evaluation\"}\n",
    "The classification metrics below are computed on the **same data used to fit the model**, giving an **optimistic** picture of predictive performance. In a prediction-focused workflow you would split data into training and test sets before reporting these metrics. Here our primary goal is **inference** — understanding which predictors are associated with survival — and the classification metrics illustrate how a fitted logistic regression translates into a classifier.\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "We classify $\\hat{Y}_i = 1$ if $\\hat{\\pi}_i > 0.5$ and summarise performance with the confusion matrix and ROC curve."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "19f566d4",
